    "evidence_text": "Luna Park was an amusement park in Coney Island, Brooklyn, in New York City that opened in 1903.\n\n It was just north of the boardwalk, near the former Luna Park amusement complex, and across from the current New York Aquarium.\n\nLuna Park, Coney Island (2010)\n\nLuna Park is the name of an amusement park in the neighborhood of Coney Island, Brooklyn in New York City that opened on May 29, 2010 at the former site of Astroland, an amusement park that had been in operation for 46 years.\n\n It was named after the original 1903 Luna Park which existed until 1944 on a site just north of the current park's 1000 Surf Avenue location.\n\n Steeplechase was Coney Island's longest lasting park.\n\nDreamland (amusement park)\n\nDreamland was an ambitious amusement park at Coney Island, Brooklyn, New York City from 1904 to 1911.\n\n It was the last, and considered the grandest, of the three original iconic large parks built on Coney Island, the other two being Steeplechase Park and Luna Park.",
